+# TASK-028 (round 2): Windowless launches enforced by the bridge: the launcher's driver kind and the suite's frozen default
+
+## Objective
+
+This is round 2 of TASK-028. It corrects round 1 in place. Round 1's work is already in this checkout (branch `task-028`): the `--kind driver` of `bridge/cursor-bridge/bridge-run.py`, the snapshot `bridge/cursor-bridge/windowless-default.snapshot.md`, the rearranged `tests/conftest.py`, the `Windowless test suite` floor in `bridge/cursor-bridge/conformance-check.py`, the allow rule and their tests. Both reviews rejected round 1. The security audit found two ways around the driver kind's path check: a link placed before a `..` component, and a directory named `x.py`. Review A found that the conformance tests do not catch the removal of a token, that the rows are not compared whole, and that the driver's logged `head` can carry an argument. Both found that the floor's configuration reading can crash the whole conformance check, and that `testpaths` can point outside the project. This round closes those findings, adds four hardening points from the audit and five smaller corrections from Review A. Everything else round 1 built stays as it is. The increment's purpose is unchanged. On 2026-10-19/20 the owner's computer crashed during a flood of terminal windows while a builder ran the test suite (ISS-011). The owner decided that the fix lives in the bridge. The launcher starts every heavy run windowless, a mutation run included (`--kind driver`), and the conformance check reports whether a project's pytest suite carries the bridge's frozen windowless default. The background for each correction is in the two review files, `run/supervisor/task028-reviewA-r1.md` and `run/supervisor/task028-security-r1.md`. Read them if you want the reviewers' wording. This brief is the instruction, and where it differs from a review, the brief governs.
+
+Satisfies: R-039 — Windowless launches are enforced by the bridge for every project, never by a per-project fix: every heavy run of the loop (a builder, a project's test suite, a mutation run) starts through the launcher (`bridge-run.py`) in the background, which starts it with no window so that every process it creates inherits that unless it detaches itself; and every project's test suite whose runner the bridge ships a default for carries the bridge's frozen windowless default (FIX-001's `tests/conftest.py` default, shipped as a snapshot; pytest in release B, the Node runners' default deferred), reported by the conformance check as a floor.
+
+## Scope
+
+One brief carries one increment's scope; work that needs a second scope is a second brief, never a second section here.
+
+Files and directories you may create or modify:
+- bridge/cursor-bridge/bridge-run.py
+- bridge/cursor-bridge/conformance-check.py
+- bridge/cursor-bridge/windowless-default.snapshot.md
+- bridge/cursor-bridge/settings.bridge.json
+- bridge/cursor-bridge/MANIFEST.json (regenerated only, by the command in Constraints)
+- tests/conftest.py
+- tests/test_bridge_run_driver.py
+- tests/test_conformance_windowless.py
+- tests/test_allowlist.py
+- docs/cli-reference.json
+- docs/CLI_REFERENCE.md
+- docs/BUILDER_NOTES.md
+- handoff/TASK-028-r2-report.md
+
+Do not modify anything else.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- .env and anything under secrets/
+- CI configuration (`.github/`, `.githooks/`)
+- docs/ and handoff/, except the files the Scope section names. That includes `handoff/TASK-028.md`, `handoff/TASK-028-r1-report.md`, this brief and the two review files under `run/supervisor/`: read them, do not edit them.
+- `bridge/cursor-bridge/mutation-run.py`: it is TASK-031's. Do not create it, not even as a stub. The launcher accepts its path whether or not the file exists.
+- `bridge/cursor-bridge/loop-guard.py` and its `KIND_CEILING` (TASK-029), the machine-wide slot (TASK-029), and every text file of the loop: `delegation-loop.md`, `supervisor.md`, `calibrate-bridge.md`, `Cursor-Project-Configuration.md`, `Known-Pitfalls.md` and the agents (TASK-030).
+- `calibration_workflows_grades`, `judge_workflows_line` and the `Workflows line` / `Workflows classification` / `Unwritten trait` floors in `conformance-check.py` (TASK-024). Leave them byte-for-byte unchanged. Leave every other floor of `conformance-check.py` unchanged too.
+- `project.json` and the conformance check's `project.json` NOTEs.
+- `tests/test_tests_windowless.py`: do not edit it. It must stay green.
+- Any other test file, including the existing conformance and bridge-run tests. They must keep passing unchanged.
+- **Findings not taken in this round.** The supervisor records these in `docs/HARDENING.md`. Do not fix them, and do not write tests for them:
+  - the interpreter-name canonicalisation: `head_of` strips `.exe`/`.cmd` anywhere in the name, and `resolve` may run a `.cmd` through `cmd.exe`. It affects the test kind too.
+  - the allow rule also matching a command with a second `--` (shared with the test kind's rule).
+  - a `.venv` interpreter reached through a link.
+  - the ambiguity of exit 1 meaning a healthy driver run. That is TASK-031's contract (`mutation-run.py` exits 2 or more on an internal error); this round keeps exits 0 and 1 healthy.
+- The round-1 test `test_r039_tools_ignore_snapshot_md` stays as it is. This round asks for no change to it.
+
+## Context
+
+**Development data.** The inventory's decision, copied verbatim: "Development data: the dev build is the Workspace sources under `bridge/`; a session in the repo always runs the *installed* bridge (`~/.claude`), never the one being edited, and installs reach running projects only through the owner's install run sheet". So the tests run the Workspace's `bridge/cursor-bridge/*.py` by file path, never the installed copy under the real `~/.claude`. Every launcher run in a test uses a temporary folder as its working folder, because `write_log` writes `run/launcher/runs.jsonl` wherever a `run/` folder exists, and the Workspace has one. `tests/conftest.py`'s autouse fixture `home_of_the_tests` sets `HOME` and `USERPROFILE` to a temporary folder for every test. So `os.path.expanduser("~")`, in the test process and in any child that copies `os.environ`, resolves to that temporary home. Nothing reads or writes the owner's real home.
+
+**Security context.** ASVS level 2 (INVENTORY, Decisions: "The builder's secure-coding rule is ASVS level 2"). `.cursor/rules/secure-coding.mdc` is in force for you. The trust boundary is the launcher's allow rule, `"Bash(python ~/.claude/cursor-bridge/bridge-run.py --limit * --kind driver -- *)"` in `bridge/cursor-bridge/settings.bridge.json`. It lets the supervisor's session run any command after `--` without asking the owner, so the launcher's own check of the driver form is the only control between that rule and arbitrary code. That check fails closed: anything it cannot positively accept is refused before any process starts. The audit's precondition holds: whoever can create a link in `run/supervisor/` can also write a `.py` there. The control's promise is still exact: the program that runs is the file that was checked, it lies inside `run/supervisor/` with no link on the way, or it is the installed `mutation-run.py`. A second boundary is the conformance check, which must read only the project's own files and print no absolute path (rule 54).
+
