+# TASK-028 (round 3): Windowless launches enforced by the bridge: the launcher's driver kind and the suite's frozen default
+
+## Objective
+
+This is round 3 of TASK-028, the increment's last ordinary round. It corrects round 2 in place. Round 2's work is already in this checkout (branch `task-028`, commit d8cad91): the hardened `--kind driver` of `bridge/cursor-bridge/bridge-run.py`, the reworked `Windowless test suite` floor of `bridge/cursor-bridge/conformance-check.py`, and their tests. Review A rejected round 2 on one Blocking finding: the alternate-data-stream test never creates the stream, so it passes with the `:` rule removed, and round 2's report claimed that mutant as caught. Review A and the security audit both found that a deeply nested `pyproject.toml` or `package.json` crashes the conformance check with a traceback (`RecursionError`), and that a `testpaths` root or the default `tests/` reached through a link makes the floor read a `conftest.py` outside the project. This round closes those three, plus four of the audit's advisories in this increment's own code (the "other runner" word printed raw, a hard link under `run/supervisor/`, a link walk that fails open on an error, a rooted program token without its drive) and four smaller corrections from Review A. Everything else round 2 built stays as it is. After this round, work goes back only for behaviour against the brief, security, data integrity, a defeated safety mechanism or a failing test, so build exactly what is written here. The background for each finding is in the two round-2 review files, `run/supervisor/task028-reviewA-r2.md` and `run/supervisor/task028-security-r2.md`. Read them for the reviewers' wording. This brief is the instruction, and where it differs from a review, the brief governs. The increment's purpose is unchanged. On 2026-10-19/20 the owner's computer crashed during a flood of terminal windows while a builder ran the test suite (ISS-011). The owner decided that the fix lives in the bridge: the launcher starts every heavy run windowless, a mutation run included (`--kind driver`), and the conformance check reports whether a project's pytest suite carries the bridge's frozen windowless default.
+
+Satisfies: R-039 — Windowless launches are enforced by the bridge for every project, never by a per-project fix: every heavy run of the loop (a builder, a project's test suite, a mutation run) starts through the launcher (`bridge-run.py`) in the background, which starts it with no window so that every process it creates inherits that unless it detaches itself; and every project's test suite whose runner the bridge ships a default for carries the bridge's frozen windowless default (FIX-001's `tests/conftest.py` default, shipped as a snapshot; pytest in release B, the Node runners' default deferred), reported by the conformance check as a floor.
